    "url": "https://github.com/1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM/pull/1448",
    "body": "Block-scaled FP8 inputs with 9–32 rows could reconstruct the full weight matrix, while the standard no-copy provider bypassed the proposed chunked dispatcher. This integration connects the compiled provider, preserves the small-row reduction order and retains policy-controlled rollback/configuration fallback. It also corrects requested-architecture selection and running-device gating for activation quantization builds.\n\nValidation on host 54633: the isolated full SM70 _C build passed without replacing the installed runtime; 186 native GPU checks and five real-provider dynamic-compile/CUDA Graph checks passed. The CMake architecture matrix, fusion selector tests, changed-file pre-commit and GitHub CI passed.\n\n**End-to-end qualification failed; do not merge.** With the original default tuning, 67-request workload-before-GSM ordering, seed and 768-token limit, GSM8K-200 scored 192/200 versus the 193/200 release-native baseline and 194/200 accepted Python integration. The additional baseline-correct failure is question 153, which ended with finish_reason=length. Raw results, full responses and comparison are preserved under /home/ymzx/pr-audit-20261109 on 54633. The fixed 2K probe was stable within the boot but its text differed across the release/new-DSO comparison; accepted drafts increased 373→377 and rounds changed 141→136. NVFP4 runtime tuning remained enabled, so this does not isolate the cause or establish a speedup.\n\nThis draft deliberately preserves the failing gate rather than promoting component checks to whole-model acceptance. Before promotion, isolate complete-build/native/tuning differences using matched controls and pass the original quality and acceptance gates. Original #1069 and #1322 heads are parents; #1187 tuning-default changes are excluded. Prepared and audited with Codex.",
